Troubleshooting Tips
Issue: ImportError for sklearn or pandas

Solution: Ensure virtual environment is activated: source venv/bin/activate
Issue: Models show poor performance (F1 < 0.5)

Check contamination parameter matches actual anomaly ratio
Verify data generation includes sufficient anomalies
Ensure proper train/test split if implemented
Issue: Visualization files not created

Check matplotlib backend: Add matplotlib.use('Agg') before importing pyplot
Verify write permissions in directory
Issue: Memory errors with large datasets

Reduce n_samples in data generation
Process data in batches for evaluation
